> I have managed to acquire a VAXstation 3100 M38. I do not know if it works, 
> but it does power up and the diagnostic lights on the back panel light up. I 
> do not have a VAXstation monitor and want to connect my PC running a 
> terminal emulator to the console port. I have a DECconnect Office Cable and 
> the relevant adapters to convert to D-sub, and the cable is plugged into the 
> printer port on the VAX.
> 
> I am not having much luck, I have a breakout box which shows the VAX 
> asserting DSR and DCD, but I do not get any characters back from the VAX, 
> nor does it react to me hitting ENTER. Assuming that the machine is working, 
> two things could be wrong, 1) I need to tell the machine to use the console 
> rather than the monitor, but I am told that if there is no monitor attached 
> then it should use the printer/console port anyway 2) I do not have the 
> right port settings, I have tried all speeds from 110 up to 9600, always no 
> parity and 8 bit, what settings should I be using?
> 
> Can anyone offer any suggestions?

On the back of the 3100 M38, there is a little switch labeled S3.  Not 
all the cases have a hole in the back for this switch.  You may need to 
open the case to find it.

One position select the graphics head for the console and the other 
selects the printer (I think) port for the console.

No the 3100 M38, you need to have a keyboard attached if you want VMS to 
license it as a VAXstation.  This is true even if you are using a 
terminal or PC as the console.  If you don't have a keyboard attached, 
it will be identified as a VAXserver.

Good luck!

